   "slug": "dancepunk",
   "name": "Dancepunk",
   "zh": "",
   "scene": "Eurotrash",
   "emerged": "early 00s",
   "aka": "Dance-punk, Discopunk, New Rave, Punk Funk, Electropunk",
   "paras": [
    {
     "en": "Dancepunk or Discopunk is the cousin to Indie -- punk bands with synthesizers. Or it's what happens when you take Electroclash and remove the Electro. You would think that it would revert back to just plain Synthpop and in some cases it did, but true to its name Dancepunk likes to keep the \"punk\" even though its audience is mostly hipsters.",
     "zh": "Dancepunk（舞曲朋克），又叫 Discopunk（迪斯科朋克），是 Indie 的表亲——拿着合成器的朋克乐队。换个说法：把 Electroclash 里的 Electro 抽掉，剩下的就是它。你可能会以为抽掉之后就变回纯粹的 Synthpop 了，有些情况下确实如此；但顾名思义，Dancepunk 喜欢留着那个「朋克」，尽管它的听众大多是文青。"
    },
    {
     "en": "Its alternative name, Discopunk, has its origins in late 70s Britain to refer to Punk bands that went Disco (a heresy in some circles) but not New Wave (it's complicated... think of an upbeat Joy Division). It doesn't actually have anything to do with modern Dancepunk but the names are interchangeable so evidently some UK music writers think there is a correlation. There isn't.",
     "zh": "它的另一个名字 Discopunk 源自 70 年代末的英国，用来指那些转去做迪斯科的朋克乐队（在某些圈子里这属于异端），但又不是新浪潮（这事挺绕……你可以想象成一支欢快版的 Joy Division）。它和现代的 Dancepunk 其实毫无关系，但两个名字被当成可以互换，显然有些英国乐评人觉得两者之间存在关联。并没有。"
    },
    {
     "en": "If you hate electronic music, Dancepunk is probably the only electronic genre you may somewhat tolerate. While a number of famous bands (Franz Ferdinand, The Killers, hell even Gorillaz) have been considered Dancepunk at one time or another, the band that really put the \"dance\" in Dancepunk was LCD Soundsystem with their hit track that confused everyone into thinking Dancepunk was a club and rave thing: Daft Punk Is Playing At My House (a-my house-ah). In a classic case of false advertising, the song doesn't have anything resembling Daft Punk in it.",
     "zh": "如果你讨厌电子音乐，Dancepunk 可能是你勉强能接受的唯一一种电子流派。不少著名乐队（Franz Ferdinand、The Killers，甚至 Gorillaz）都曾被算作 Dancepunk，但真正把「dance」注入 Dancepunk 的，是 LCD Soundsystem——他们那首让所有人误以为 Dancepunk 是俱乐部和锐舞圈的事的热门单曲《Daft Punk Is Playing At My House》（a-my house-ah）。这是虚假宣传的经典案例：这首歌里没有任何东西听起来像 Daft Punk。"
    },
    {
     "en": "(wouldn't be the first time that happened. For instance, there's Panic! At The Disco, a band that plays music that is neither Disco nor high-anxiety inducing)",
     "zh": "（这种事也不是头一回了。比如 Panic! At The Disco，这支乐队玩的音乐既不是 Disco，也引不起高度焦虑。）"
    },
    {
     "en": "LCD Soundsystem and their label Death From Above aggressively foisted this sound upon an unsuspecting club culture and the genre was picked up by other bands who recognized that live music was on the outs, guitars were d&eacute;class&eacute;, and a steady beat was necessary if you wanted the DJ to drop your record in the club.",
     "zh": "LCD Soundsystem 和他们的厂牌 Death From Above 把这套声音强行塞给了毫无防备的俱乐部文化，随后被其他乐队接手——这些乐队都看明白了：现场音乐正在失势，吉他已经掉价，想让 DJ 在俱乐部里放你的唱片，你就得有一个稳定的节拍。"
    },
    {
     "en": "Like any Punk, Punk-derived, Punk-inspired or Punk-spawned form of music, Dancepunk is irresistably drawn toward selling out. It was the first Millenial genre to spread best via commercial advertising -- mostly car companies, telcoms, tech coms, or any other corporation that tries too hard to appeal to young urban trendsetters by being totally with it and down with the scene, man.",
     "zh": "和任何一种朋克、朋克衍生、朋克启发或朋克催生的音乐一样，Dancepunk 无法抗拒「出卖自己」的诱惑。它是第一个主要通过商业广告传播的千禧年流派——客户大多是汽车公司、电信公司、科技公司，以及任何拼命想讨好年轻都市潮流人士、想显得「完全跟得上、特别懂圈子」的企业。"
    },
    {
     "en": "This is the bottom of the Guide. If you're one of those obsessive-compulsive completist types who has to go through everything sequentially and this is the last genre you're visiting -- like you just have to read every page in a Choose Your Own Adventure book in numerical order -- that's probably not the best use of your time. Have you considered crystal meth?",
     "zh": "这里是本指南的底部。如果你属于那种必须按顺序把所有内容都过一遍的强迫症收藏型人格，而这里恰好是你访问的最后一个流派——就像你非得按数字顺序读完一整本《选择你自己的冒险》——那你大概把时间用错了地方。你考虑过冰毒吗？"
    },
    {
     "en": "Ish.",
     "zh": "Ish."
    }
   ],
