     "file": "dat.png",
     "caption": "A DAT is a Digital Audio Tape, a superior format to the analog cassette tape that was the consumer format of choice in the 80s. It didn't catch on due to piracy concerns and because CDs were just around the corner anyway, but it was prized by studio producers and engineers for its hi-fidelity. It's still often used for mastering and recording today."
